From: j7
Subject: j7: read the display controller and the whole clock bank

The display controller dump never printed: it was guarded by (parsed && decon), and

PE_parse_boot_argn() returns false when the argument is absent, so the default of 1

could never turn it on. The tearing fix needs those registers.

The clock PLLs read 1804/1332/1599 MHz while the CPU measures 899, which is the memory

PLL halved, so the ARM clock is a mux and a divider somewhere in CMU_MIF. No driver in

this tree publishes which register, so dump the whole 4 KB and read it off. Also log

whether the row shadow exists: without it every present rewrites all 1920 rows.

Co-Authored-By: dipa-studio <183933817+dipa-studio@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -326,6 +326,9 @@
 		if (fShadow != NULL) {
 			bzero(fShadow, (vm_size_t)fLogicalW * fLogicalH * 4);
 		}
+		/* Without it every present rebuilds and restores all 1920 panel rows even when the
+		 * frame did not change, which is most of a copy that measured 35 ms. */
+		IOLog("A5XELTE FB: row shadow %s\n", fShadow != NULL ? "on" : "off");
 		if (fCanvas == NULL) {
 			IOLog("SWEET FB: no canvas surface, clients keep the panel\n");
 		} else {
@@ -415,7 +418,10 @@
 		 * tearing. Read its window 0 state before touching it, so a double buffer and a
 		 * flip at vsync can be programmed against real values instead of guesses. */
 		int decon = 1;
-		if (PE_parse_boot_argn("j7decon", &decon, sizeof(decon)) && decon != 0) {
+		/* Default on: PE_parse_boot_argn() returns false when the argument is absent, so
+		 * "parsed && decon" left the dump off on every boot that did not pass it. */
+		PE_parse_boot_argn("j7decon", &decon, sizeof(decon));
+		if (decon != 0) {
 			IOMemoryDescriptor *desc = IOMemoryDescriptor::withPhysicalAddress(
 			    0x14830000ULL, 0x1000, kIODirectionNone);
 			IOMemoryMap *map = desc != NULL ? desc->map(kIOMapInhibitCache) : NULL;
@@ -464,6 +470,18 @@
 					IOLog("A5XELTE CLK: %s PLL_CON0=%08x M=%u P=%u S=%u en=%u -> %llu kHz\n",
 					    plls[i].name, con0, m, pd, s, (con0 >> 31) & 1, khz);
 				}
+				/* The three PLLs are 1804/1332/1599 MHz and the CPU measures 899, which is
+				 * the memory PLL halved: the ARM clock is a mux and a divider somewhere in
+				 * this bank, and no driver in this tree publishes which. Dump the whole
+				 * 4 KB so the mux and divisor can be read off real values. */
+				for (uint32_t o = 0; o < 0x1000; o += 0x40) {
+					IOLog("A5XELTE CLK: %03x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x "
+					    "%08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x\n", o,
+					    c[o / 4 + 0], c[o / 4 + 1], c[o / 4 + 2], c[o / 4 + 3],
+					    c[o / 4 + 4], c[o / 4 + 5], c[o / 4 + 6], c[o / 4 + 7],
+					    c[o / 4 + 8], c[o / 4 + 9], c[o / 4 + 10], c[o / 4 + 11],
+					    c[o / 4 + 12], c[o / 4 + 13], c[o / 4 + 14], c[o / 4 + 15]);
+				}
 			} else {
 				IOLog("A5XELTE CLK: no map\n");
 			}
